Reused work
-----------
Ideas and a small amount of code in CodePuff were adapted from the author's own project Metacognition
(https://github.com/luizbizzio/metacognition, Apache License 2.0, same copyright holder):

  - the approach of observing a coding agent through its hook events and recognizing what a tool call is;
  - the idea of a small pixel critter drawn from lit blocks (a bright top, a front, a shaded side).
    The "Claude" character in CodePuff is a new drawing in that spirit, rebuilt on CodePuff's own pixel canvas;
    no artwork file was copied.

Nothing from Metacognition's reflection, strategy-learning, advice-injection or verification-policy code is included.

Third-party code and assets
---------------------------
CodePuff has no runtime dependencies. The animations, color logic, Alpha and the "Claude" critter are drawn in
code for this project. The artwork of Classic, Foxy, Bot, Slime, Mage and Penny (src/core/art/sprites.js) is converted to pixel
art, by scripts/sprites/*.py, from character images that the project owner created with an AI image generator (OpenAI's
GPT image generation) from the owner's own designs. The owner states that they hold the rights to use and distribute these
images under the generator's terms; anyone redistributing CodePuff should read those terms themselves. The images are not in
this repository, so src/core/art/sprites.js cannot be regenerated from it alone (see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, "Keep the sheets").
The sound clips (assets/sounds) are synthesized by scripts/make-sounds.mjs and are original.

